tion {:value "255701"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255714"} "Kayak Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255727"} "Kayak Fours, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255739"} "Canadian Singles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255751"} "Canadian Singles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255757"} "Canadian Doubles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255763"} "Canadian Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255769"} "Kayak Singles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "255775"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "255782"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "255441"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "255581"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "255783"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "255925"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "256068"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "256204"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "256317"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "258743"} "2008"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/159"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Kayak Singles, 500 metres, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "6 – 10 August 1984"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/604"} "Lake Casitas, Los Padres National Forest, California"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/255675"} "19 from 19 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Unlike the 1980 American-led boycott, which had had a limited impact on the canoeing events, the Soviet boycott of the 1984 Summer Olympics severely depleted the field in the sport. This was undeniable in the men’s K-1 500, for the defending Olympic and four-time World Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/10999"} "Vladimir Parfenovich"] " of the Soviet Union was absent, as were the East Germans, who had taken silver and bronze at the 1982 and 1983 Worlds respectively. This left three major contenders at the Games: New Zealand’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/10430"} "Ian Ferguson"] ", the 1983 World runner-up, " [:a {:href "/athletes/10787"} "Lars-Erik Moberg"] " of Sweden, the 1981 and 1982 World bronze medalist, and Romania’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/10581"} "Vasile Dîba"] " who, among many international accolades, had been the 1976 Olympic champion and 1980 bronze medalist."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Dîba earned the opening round’s fastest time as he defeated Ferguson, while Moberg and Yugoslavia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/11201"} "Milan Janić"] " took the other heats. Ferguson then posted the fastest time in the semi-finals, besting Janić in the process, while Moberg came in second to France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/9606"} "Bernard Brégeon"] " in other heat and Dîba captured the third. As the crews approached the finish line in the medal round, Ferguson, Moberg, Brégeon, and Dîba were clustered together and finished in that order with less than a second between them. Brégeon would win another Olympic medal, silver, in the K-2 1000, while Ferguson and Moberg’s rivalry would continue into the K-2 500 and the K-4 1000, where the Swede would be runner-up twice more to the New Zealander."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Rep"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "126"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/10430"} "Ian Ferguson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countri